      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group 2 elements, beryllium, magnesium, calcium, strontium, barium and radium, are s-block elements. They are called the alkaline earth metals because they are metallic and occur in the earth's crust, and their reactivity lies between that of the very reactive alkali metals and the less reactive transition metals. Calcium and magnesium are among the eight most abundant elements of the earth's crust."
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "note",
            "title": "Did you know?",
            "text": "Beryllium is used to make copper alloys harder for aerospace materials, magnesium is part of chlorophyll, and magnesium, calcium, strontium and barium give fireworks their bright colours."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "All Group 2 elements have two electrons in their outermost s subshell (ns2), so their chemical properties are similar, but properties change steadily down the group. The trends in melting point and density depend on the different ways the metal atoms are packed."
